  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,1\\,|=1\n$$",
